<title>AUSTRIA: ALPINE SKIING-COMPAGNONI WINS WORLD CUP SLALOM.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-COMPAGNONI WINS WORLD CUP SLALOM.</headline>
<dateline>SEMMERING, Austria 1996-12-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deborah Compagnoni of Italy won a women's World Cup slalom on Sunday with a combined time for two runs of one minute 42.94 seconds, according to provisional results.</p>
<p>Patricia Chauvet of France was second in 1:43.99 and Claudia Riegler of New Zealand third in 1:45.65, also provisionally.</p>
